# netbsd14 — NetBSD 1.4.1 i386 (1999). Reset = loadvm golden on disk.qcow2, the
# only block device (rule 6: golden + /opt/qemu-beos binary + device set are one).
# Checkpoint: golden RE-BAKED 2026-09-03 08:55:46 under /opt/qemu-beos on the
# retronet device set (second ne2k_pci on tap netbsd14rn0, and restrict=on on the
# SLIRP netdev) with the noaccel XF86Config, VM_SIZE 41.8 MiB, VM_CLOCK
# 0000:00:58.659; restore proven (scene 5.9 s after launch+cont, X handshake on
# the loopback forward answers 1 in 1.0 s, and mICQ signs back on ~45 s later
# unattended even when the gateway had already reaped the stale session).
SH_RESET_MODE=loadvm
SH_GOLDEN_SNAPSHOT=golden
SH_GOLDEN_STATE_DISK=/data/vms/streamhost/stations/netbsd14/disk.qcow2
SH_FIXTURE_DESC=NetBSD 1.4.1 twm desktop (XFree86 3.3.3.1 SVGA on Cirrus, 1024x768x8, KHMIN kernel): xterm 'NetBSD 1.4.1' with a root prompt over the origin, Calculator, xclock, and along the bottom the two retronet windows — 'ICQ - mICQ' (mICQ 0.4.12 signed in as UIN 17600, HiveBot online in the contact list) and 'Web Browser - Lynx' (Lynx 2.8.2 on http://search.retronet/). Pointer motion absolute through the guest X server (x11warp), buttons + keys over PS/2.
# 60/60, not the 40/40 fleet floor: at 40/40 the guest drops ~8 % of characters (3 of 37,
# measured 2026-09-03 with labctl type); qmp-type at >=80 ms gaps typed the alphabet clean.
SH_KEY_MIN_HOLD_MS=60
SH_KEY_MIN_GAP_MS=60
NETBSD14_QEMU=/opt/qemu-beos/bin/qemu-system-x86_64
# Pointer: motion via XWarpPointer + XQueryPointer readback on the guest's X
# server, reached through the launcher's loopback SLIRP forward (6076 -> 6000).
# The golden carries `xhost +10.0.2.2`. Buttons/keys: D-Bus PS/2 (default path).
SH_INPUT_BACKEND=x11warp
SH_X11WARP_DISPLAY=127.0.0.1:76
SH_X11WARP_TRACE=off
SH_CURSOR_SCALE=1.0
# Retronet: ne1 is the tap netbsd14rn0 on vmbr-rn, static 10.99.0.32/24, guard
# chain NETBSD14RN-IN. It carries the guest's ONLY resolver (10.99.0.2) and its
# ONLY default route (10.99.0.2, /etc/mygate) — see docs/lab/retronet/STATION-netbsd14.md.
# ne0 (SLIRP) keeps the 10.0.2.15/24 address and nothing else: the launcher runs
# that netdev with restrict=on, so the guest can no longer route into the host
# stack via 10.0.2.2 or resolve via 10.0.2.3, while the host-initiated loopback
# forward 6076->10.0.2.15:6000 still reaches the guest's X server (verified after
# the change: the raw X connection-setup handshake still answers 1).
# SH_X11WARP_DISPLAY above is therefore deliberately NOT pointed at
# 10.99.0.32:6000: the retronet link is fail-closed toward labhost, so an X
# connection from the host to the guest over vmbr-rn would be a hole in the
# containment chain, while the SLIRP forward is host-initiated and local.
